                <pb facs="1305" n="1295" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.91293/10–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-11T09:00:00+08:00">October 11, 1949—9
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 11—1:11 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4257. With suspension activities local foreign press, news agencies and
                    correspondents (reContel 4207, October 7), and [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >sic</hi>] news items used on VOA or press handouts based on information from
                    this office not attributable other sources will presumably be considered by
                    Communist authorities to have originated from this office. In view delicate
                    situation with respect maintenance our radio contact, suggest extreme
                    desirability close scrutiny any VOA and other releases concerning Shanghai area
                    or otherwise readily traceable to this ConGen. Special caution desirable on
                    anything which hypersensitive Communists might construe as of military
                    significance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
